; dense-token-handle.fk — ONE Form cell for the whole dense-decoder family, loop in the body.
;
; llama-token-handle.fk carried llama3.2:3b's decode loop home through the handle door. This cell is
; the same shape GENERALIZED, so that one body of dispatch code speaks for every dense GGUF this
; machine holds: llama3.2:1b, MiniCPM5-1B, Nanbeige4.2-3B, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-32B, the Qwen2.5
; pair. Not one geometry number is typed in — every difference between those files is READ from that
; file's own header:
;
;   arch prefix        general.architecture names the KV prefix (llama. / qwen2. / nanbeige.)
;   head_dim           <arch>.attention.key_length when present (MiniCPM5: 128 while d/nHead = 96),
;                      else embedding_length / head_count
;   rope style         llama-arch files carry ADJACENT pairs (the GGUF conversion permutes Q/K for
;                      exactly this); qwen2-family files are HALF-SPLIT (neox). The style is decided
;                      by the arch string the file declares, and both kernels are in the unit.
;   qkv bias           read from the table: blk.N.attn_q.bias present -> added after the matvec.
;                      A file without the tensor dispatches nothing (qwen2 yes, llama no).
;   loops              <arch>.num_loops (nanbeige: 2) — the SAME 22 layers applied again, with the
;                      final norm between passes (skip_loop_final_norm=0) and PER-PASS KV banks
;                      (cache slot = layer + loop * nLayer), exactly the semantics
;                      nanbeige-looped-transformer.fk proved four-way on the CPU.
;   rope freqs         rope_freqs.weight when the file carries one (llama3.2); a buffer of 1.0f the
;                      cell writes through metal_buf_write when it does not — theta then reduces to
;                      pos * base^(-i/hd), which is exactly the no-factor rope.
;   quantization       per TENSOR, from that tensor's own ggml type: Q6_K (14), Q4_K (12), Q8_0 (8)
;                      matvecs are all in the unit; F32 (0) and F16 (1) are priced for views. An
;                      unknown type prices to 0 bytes and the zero-length view refuses loudly at
;                      metal_buf_from_file rather than dispatching garbage.
;   tied embeddings    the absence of output.weight in the table, never a convention.
;
; THE KERNELS ARE THE BODY'S ATTESTANTS, and (2026-08-08) THE BODY'S NAMED TWINS. The serial
; attestants (q6k/q4k/q80/q5k/q50/q40 fused matvec — one thread per row, serial right-fold;
; form_rmsnorm_f32; form_rope_f32; form_argmax_f32) all stay in the unit and the CPU twins still
; answer to them. The DISPATCHED path took the two growths the llama lane proved on 2026-08-04
; and this stone swept family-wide on 2026-08-08, gated by the full two-prompt id stream per
; model (first-token-only is blind — this band's own M-2/M-4):
;
;   BIT-EXACT twins (equality, not epsilon): form_rmsnorm_tg_f32 inside its stated radius
;   (n <= 4096, one threadgroup; past it — qwen2-32B d=5120, 72B d=8192 — the serial attestant
;   stays because the twin there is WRONG, not slow), form_rope_pair_f32 (a thread map, hd even),
;   form_argmax_part/comb_f32 (comparison and selection only, ties still to the lowest index),
;   tpg=256 on every mode-0 dispatch, and concurrent batches whose hazards THIS CELL declares
;   per dispatch (barrier_before = "must I see my predecessors' writes").
;
;   EPSILON-BEARING twins, the reassociation ARGUED and WITNESSED: every matvec dispatches the
;   LANE kernel — one SIMD group of 32 per row, lane l folding columns l, l+32, ... with k
;   counting DOWN (the within-lane fold keeps tb-dot's right-fold direction), per-block scale
;   invariants hoisted (exact same f32 values, association untouched), metal::simd_sum the ONE
;   reassociation. qk-matvec-lane.fk derives the bound: |y_lane - y_serial| <=
;   (cols + ceil(cols/32) + 32) * 2^-24 * SUM|w_j*x_j|, valid for ANY simd_sum tree since 32
;   terms cannot exceed depth 31. Q6_K/Q4_K lane kernels are that cell's own; Q8_0's is
;   q8-0-msl.fk's; Q5_K/Q5_0/Q4_0 are transcribed HERE from their attestants' own weight
;   decompositions, split at the block invariant and nowhere else. The witnessed gate: the full
;   16-id stream for two prompts, per model, equal before and after (2026-08-08, this stone).
;
; Two kernels are this cell's own and both are transcriptions, not inventions: dth-copy-msl is
; the identity with a shifted destination (the KV-cache move the door's fixed-offset binding
; makes necessary — llama-token-handle.fk's finding, kept), and dth-neox-msl is form_rope_f32's
; arithmetic with the pair layout (j, j+rd/2) instead of (i, i+1) and the frequency exponent
; 2j/rd — the half-split rotation the qwen2 family declares. fp contraction is OFF by pragma in
; the emitted text, the fix fk-metal-carrier.m's own header says belongs to the Form cell.
;
; THE TENSOR TABLE IS WALKED ONCE. egg-find-tensor re-walks the header per lookup — measured O(n^2)
; at 255 tensors (~74 s of setup) and 771 tensors would pay ~9x that. dth-table carries the cursor
; through the tensor infos exactly once and keeps (name type d0 d1 dataoff bytes) rows; every later
; lookup is a list scan. The same one-walk shape l3d-pieces uses for the vocabulary, applied to the
; table.
;
; THE TOKENIZER IS THE ATTESTANT'S, PORTED AND SAID PLAINLY: greedy LONGEST-MATCH over the file's
; own vocabulary, not BPE merge order — metal_first_token.sh states this about itself at its encode
; function and the body owes the same statement. gpt2-model vocabs go through the byte-level
; alphabet FORWARD (text byte -> substitute codepoint -> UTF-8, the exact inverse of
; llama3-detokenize.fk's map); llama-model (SentencePiece) vocabs go through the space -> U+2581
; convention. BOS is the file's tokenizer.ggml.bos_token_id, prepended when the file's
; add_bos_token says so (a BOOL KV, type 7 — read as such, not misread through a u32 door).
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk form-stdlib/str-byte-at.fk form-stdlib/equireach.fk form-stdlib/format-arith.fk form-stdlib/f16-decode.fk form-stdlib/q6k-dequant.fk form-stdlib/q4k-dequant.fk form-stdlib/equireach-gguf.fk form-stdlib/q6k-msl.fk form-stdlib/q4k-msl.fk form-stdlib/q8-0-msl.fk form-stdlib/q5-msl.fk form-stdlib/transformer-numerics.fk form-stdlib/transformer-block.fk form-stdlib/llama-numerics.fk form-stdlib/gguf-meta.fk form-stdlib/trig.fk form-stdlib/tensor-ir.fk form-stdlib/jit-tensor-emit.fk form-stdlib/llama-decode-msl.fk form-stdlib/qk-matvec-split.fk form-stdlib/qk-matvec-lane.fk form-stdlib/metal-door.fk form-stdlib/llama3-detokenize.fk
;
; Proven by: form/native/metal/tests/dense-family-band.fk

(do
    ; ================= the translation unit =================
    (defn dth-copy-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device const float* s [[buffer(0)]], device float* d [[buffer(1)]], constant uint& n [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& doff [[buffer(3)]], uint i [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (i >= n) return; d[doff + i] = s[i]; }")))

    ; Half-split rope: pair (j, j+rd/2) of the first rd dims of each head, theta = pos *
    ; base^(-2j/rd) / fr[j]. Per head, serial over pairs — form_rope_f32's own shape and rounding
    ; discipline (named temporaries, the recipe's fpow/fsin/fcos), only the LAYOUT differs.
    (defn dth-neox-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device float* v [[buffer(0)]], device const float* fr [[buffer(1)]], constant uint& nh [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& hd [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& rd [[buffer(4)]], constant uint& pos [[buffer(5)]], constant float& base [[buffer(6)]], uint h [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (h >= nh) return; uint o = h * hd; uint np = rd / 2u; uint j = 0; while (j < np) { float ex = (-2.0f * float(j)) / float(rd); float fq = fpow(base, ex) / fr[j]; float a = float(pos) * fq; float ca = fcos(a); float sa = fsin(a); float q0 = v[o + j]; float q1 = v[o + j + np]; float t0 = q0 * ca; float t1 = q1 * sa; v[o + j] = t0 - t1; float t2 = q0 * sa; float t3 = q1 * ca; v[o + j + np] = t2 + t3; j += 1u; } }")))

    ; Half-split rope at PAIR grain (2026-08-08, round two): dth-neox-msl's inner iteration is
    ; independent per pair (j, j+rd/2) — theta reads only (base, pos, j, rd, fr[j]) — so unrolling
    ; the per-head serial loop across nh*(rd/2) threads is a thread map, BIT FOR BIT the per-head
    ; kernel, the same argument form_rope_pair_f32 carries for adjacent pairs. RADIUS: rd even —
    ; at odd rd the serial kernel stays (its while (j < np) drops nothing, but np pairs of an odd
    ; rd do not tile; the carrier checks).
    (defn dth-neox-pair-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device float* v [[buffer(0)]], device const float* fr [[buffer(1)]], constant uint& nh [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& hd [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& rd [[buffer(4)]], constant uint& pos [[buffer(5)]], constant float& base [[buffer(6)]], uint gid [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { uint np = rd / 2u; if (gid >= nh * np) return; uint h = gid / np; uint j = gid - h * np; uint o = h * hd; float ex = (-2.0f * float(j)) / float(rd); float fq = fpow(base, ex) / fr[j]; float a = float(pos) * fq; float ca = fcos(a); float sa = fsin(a); float q0 = v[o + j]; float q1 = v[o + j + np]; float t0 = q0 * ca; float t1 = q1 * sa; v[o + j] = t0 - t1; float t2 = q0 * sa; float t3 = q1 * ca; v[o + j + np] = t2 + t3; }")))

    ; ---- the phi2 appendix: what a parallel-residual, LayerNorm, GELU, Q4_0 block needs ----
    ; LayerNorm with gain AND bias — mean-centered, unlike RMSNorm. One thread, the family's own
    ; Newton-50 sqrt seeded at its argument, ascending folds.
    (defn dth-ln-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device const float* x [[buffer(0)]], device const float* g [[buffer(1)]], device const float* bb [[buffer(2)]], device float* y [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& n [[buffer(4)]], constant float& eps [[buffer(5)]], uint gid [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (gid != 0u) return; float s = 0.0f; uint j = 0; while (j < n) { s = s + x[j]; j += 1; } float mean = s / float(n); float v = 0.0f; j = 0; while (j < n) { float c = x[j] - mean; v = v + c * c; j += 1; } float sdv = v / float(n) + eps; float gg = sdv; uint it = 50; while (it > 0) { it -= 1; gg = 0.5f * (gg + sdv / gg); } float inv = 1.0f / gg; j = 0; while (j < n) { y[j] = ((x[j] - mean) * inv) * g[j] + bb[j]; j += 1; } }")))

    ; GELU, tanh form, tanh through the unit's own fexp with the always-bounded e^(-2|t|) shape:
    ; e is in (0,1], so no overflow path exists and no clamp is invented.
    (defn dth-gelu-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device const float* x [[buffer(0)]], device float* y [[buffer(1)]], constant uint& n [[buffer(2)]], uint i [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (i >= n) return; float xv = x[i]; float t = 0.7978845608028654f * (xv + 0.044715f * xv * xv * xv); float at = (t < 0.0f) ? -t : t; float e = fexp(-2.0f * at); float s = (1.0f - e) / (1.0f + e); float th = (t < 0.0f) ? -s : s; y[i] = 0.5f * xv * (1.0f + th); }")))

    ; d[i] = s[soff + i] — the read-side twin of the cache move, for slicing a fused qkv.
    (defn dth-copyfrom-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device const float* s [[buffer(0)]], device float* d [[buffer(1)]], constant uint& n [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& soff [[buffer(3)]], uint i [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (i >= n) return; d[i] = s[soff + i]; }")))

    ; Q4_0: { half d; uint8 qs[16]; } — 18 bytes per 32 weights, w = d * (nib - 8). The q4k helpers
    ; are the unit's; only the weight reach is new.
    (defn dth-q40-weight-msl ()
        "static inline float q40_w(device const uchar* qb, uint idx) { uint blk = idx / 32u; uint i = idx - blk * 32u; uint b = blk * 18u; uint half_ = i / 16u; uint j = i - half_ * 16u; int qbyte = int(qb[b + 2u + j]); int nib = (half_ == 0u) ? q4k_mod(qbyte, 16) : qbyte / 16; float d = q4k_f16(int(qb[b + 0u]) + 256 * int(qb[b + 1u])); return d * float(nib - 8); } ")
    (defn dth-q40-dequant-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device const uchar* qb [[buffer(0)]], device float* w [[buffer(1)]], constant uint& off [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& n [[buffer(3)]], uint i [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (i >= n) return; w[i] = q40_w(qb, off + i); }")))
    (defn dth-q40-matvec-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device const uchar* qb [[buffer(0)]], device const float* x [[buffer(1)]], device float* y [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& rows [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& cols [[buffer(4)]], uint i [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (i >= rows) return; float acc = 0.0f; uint j = cols; while (j > 0) { j -= 1; float p = q40_w(qb, uint(i) * cols + j) * float(x[j]); acc = p + acc; } y[i] = acc; }")))

    ; ---- the three lane matvecs qk-matvec-lane.fk does not carry, same shape lane for lane:
    ; one SIMD group per row, lane l takes columns l, l+32, ..., k counting DOWN so the
    ; within-lane fold keeps tb-dot's right-fold direction, per-block invariants hoisted (exact
    ; values, association untouched), metal::simd_sum the one reassociation. The named epsilon is
    ; qk-matvec-lane.fk's own at parts=32 — (cols + ceil(cols/32) + 32) * 2^-24 * SUM|w_j*x_j| —
    ; unchanged because ANY association of 32 lane partials has depth < 32. Each weight
    ; decomposition below is that quant's own *_w body (q5-msl.fk / this cell's q40), split at
    ; the block invariant and nowhere else.
    (defn dth-q5k-lane-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device const uchar* qb [[buffer(0)]], device const float* x [[buffer(1)]], device float* y [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& rows [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& cols [[buffer(4)]], uint gid [[thread_position_in_grid]], uint lane [[thread_index_in_simdgroup]]) { uint r = gid / 32u; if (r >= rows) return; float acc = 0.0f; uint curblk = 4294967295u; uint b = 0u; float2 inv = float2(0.0f, 0.0f); uint nk = (cols > lane) ? ((cols - lane + 31u) / 32u) : 0u; uint k = nk; while (k > 0) { k -= 1; uint j = lane + k * 32u; uint idx = r * cols + j; uint blk = idx / 256u; if (blk != curblk) { curblk = blk; b = blk * 176u; inv = float2(q4k_f16(int(qb[b + 0u]) + 256 * int(qb[b + 1u])), q4k_f16(int(qb[b + 2u]) + 256 * int(qb[b + 3u]))); } int i = int(idx - blk * 256u); int c = i / 64; int within = q4k_mod(i, 64); int hf = within / 32; int l = q4k_mod(within, 32); int sj = 2 * c + hf; int qbyte = int(qb[b + 48u + uint(c * 32 + l)]); int nib = (hf == 0) ? q4k_mod(qbyte, 16) : qbyte / 16; int hb = q5k_bit(int(qb[b + 16u + uint(l)]), sj); float pr = ((inv.x * float(q4k_sc(qb, b, sj))) * float(nib + 16 * hb) - inv.y * float(q4k_mn(qb, b, sj))) * float(x[j]); acc = pr + acc; } float s = metal::simd_sum(acc); if (lane == 0) y[r] = s; }")))

    (defn dth-q50-lane-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device const uchar* qb [[buffer(0)]], device const float* x [[buffer(1)]], device float* y [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& rows [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& cols [[buffer(4)]], uint gid [[thread_position_in_grid]], uint lane [[thread_index_in_simdgroup]]) { uint r = gid / 32u; if (r >= rows) return; float acc = 0.0f; uint curblk = 4294967295u; uint b = 0u; float d = 0.0f; uint qh = 0u; uint nk = (cols > lane) ? ((cols - lane + 31u) / 32u) : 0u; uint k = nk; while (k > 0) { k -= 1; uint j = lane + k * 32u; uint idx = r * cols + j; uint blk = idx / 32u; if (blk != curblk) { curblk = blk; b = blk * 22u; d = q4k_f16(int(qb[b + 0u]) + 256 * int(qb[b + 1u])); qh = uint(qb[b + 2u]) + 256u * uint(qb[b + 3u]) + 65536u * uint(qb[b + 4u]) + 16777216u * uint(qb[b + 5u]); } uint i = idx - blk * 32u; uint half_ = i / 16u; uint sj = i - half_ * 16u; int qbyte = int(qb[b + 6u + sj]); int nib = (half_ == 0u) ? q4k_mod(qbyte, 16) : qbyte / 16; int hb = int(q50_bit(qh, i)); float pr = d * float(nib + 16 * hb - 16) * float(x[j]); acc = pr + acc; } float s = metal::simd_sum(acc); if (lane == 0) y[r] = s; }")))

    (defn dth-q40-lane-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device const uchar* qb [[buffer(0)]], device const float* x [[buffer(1)]], device float* y [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& rows [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& cols [[buffer(4)]], uint gid [[thread_position_in_grid]], uint lane [[thread_index_in_simdgroup]]) { uint r = gid / 32u; if (r >= rows) return; float acc = 0.0f; uint curblk = 4294967295u; uint b = 0u; float d = 0.0f; uint nk = (cols > lane) ? ((cols - lane + 31u) / 32u) : 0u; uint k = nk; while (k > 0) { k -= 1; uint j = lane + k * 32u; uint idx = r * cols + j; uint blk = idx / 32u; if (blk != curblk) { curblk = blk; b = blk * 18u; d = q4k_f16(int(qb[b + 0u]) + 256 * int(qb[b + 1u])); } uint i = idx - blk * 32u; uint half_ = i / 16u; uint sj = i - half_ * 16u; int qbyte = int(qb[b + 2u + sj]); int nib = (half_ == 0u) ? q4k_mod(qbyte, 16) : qbyte / 16; float pr = d * float(nib - 8) * float(x[j]); acc = pr + acc; } float s = metal::simd_sum(acc); if (lane == 0) y[r] = s; }")))

    ; ---- the FACTORED-SCALE lane matvecs (2026-08-08, round two). Round one's lane kernels
    ; still recomputed per-weight what the format prices per GROUP: Q6_K re-derived sc and the
    ; index decomposition per weight, Q4_K/Q5_K the 6-bit sc/mn chains, Q8_0/Q5_0/Q4_0 the block
    ; scale, all through div/mod helper calls and (for the K quants) the q*_f16 multiply-loop
    ; decode. qk-matvec-lane.fk's own header named the remaining distance: factor the scale OUT
    ; of the inner sum, decode with bitmasks. These six kernels take exactly that and nothing
    ; else:
    ;
    ;   * lane l owns whole SCALE GROUPS (Q8_0/Q5_0/Q4_0: the 32-weight block; Q4_K/Q5_K: the
    ;     32-weight sub-block; Q6_K: the 16-weight group) at G = l, l+32, ... — so the group's
    ;     invariants are computed ONCE per group instead of once per weight. Within-group fold
    ;     ASCENDING, group chain ascending, metal::simd_sum the one cross-lane reassociation
    ;     (any tree over 32 terms has depth < 32 — round one's argument, unchanged).
    ;   * the scale enters ONCE per group: acc += (d*sc)*SUM(q*x) [- (dmin*mn)*SUM(x) where the
    ;     format carries mins]. d*sc and dmin*mn are EXACT in f32 (f16 11-bit significand times
    ;     a <=8-bit int). For Q6_K this is pure reassociation under the SAME anchor
    ;     SUM|w_j x_j| as round one's epsilon; for Q8_0/Q5_0/Q4_0 likewise (coefficient ~2x);
    ;     for Q4_K/Q5_K the min-term DISTRIBUTION enlarges the anchor to
    ;     SUM(|ds*nib*x| + |dm*mn*x|) — stated plainly, and gated by the measured two-prompt
    ;     stream, not argued into the old bound.
    ;   * bitmask decode (& 15, >> 4, >> 2g, bit tests) replaces the div/mod helper chains —
    ;     value-identical on uchar bytes; as_type<half> replaces the q*_f16 multiply-loop —
    ;     value-identical for every finite half (q8-0-msl.fk and ds4-order-match.fk precedent).
    ;   * NOT taken: int8 activation quantization (ds4's CPU dot_q8_0_row). Its int32 block dot
    ;     is exact (32*127*128 < 2^24) — but only relative to a QUANTIZED activation, a value
    ;     change ~2^-8, no u-scale bound exists against the attestant fold. betterwrong
    ;     (corpus 951): equality wins. Activations stay f32.
    ;
    ;   * (2026-08-09, round three) a BIAS EPILOGUE rides on every lane2 kernel: when bflag=1,
    ;     lane 0 stores s + bias[r] instead of s. The attestant did the same add in its own
    ;     dispatch — matvec stored y[r], form_add_f32 read it back and added — and an f32
    ;     store/load is the identity, so the fused add is the SAME one add on the SAME two
    ;     values: a bit-exact fusion, one fenced stage fewer per biased layer. bflag=0 stores
    ;     s exactly as before; callers without a bias bind y itself at the slot and 0.
    ;
    ; The serial attestants and round one's lane kernels all STAY in the unit; these dispatch.
    (defn dth-q80-lane2-msl ()
        "kernel void form_q80_matvec_lane2_f32 (device const uchar* qb [[buffer(0)]], device const float* x [[buffer(1)]], device float* y [[buffer(2)]], device const float* bias [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& rows [[buffer(4)]], constant uint& cols [[buffer(5)]], constant uint& bflag [[buffer(6)]], uint gid [[thread_position_in_grid]], uint lane [[thread_index_in_simdgroup]]) { uint r = gid / 32u; if (r >= rows) return; uint nb = cols / 32u; ulong rowbase = (ulong)r * (ulong)nb * 34ul; float acc = 0.0f; for (uint b = lane; b < nb; b += 32u) { device const uchar* bp = qb + rowbase + (ulong)b * 34ul; ushort h = (ushort)bp[0] | ((ushort)bp[1] << 8); float d = float(as_type<half>(h)); device const uchar* qs = bp + 2u; device const float* xb = x + b * 32u; float sumq = 0.0f; for (uint i = 0u; i < 32u; i += 4u) { char4 w = char4(*(device const packed_char4*)(qs + i)); float4 xv = float4(*(device const packed_float4*)(xb + i)); sumq = sumq + float(w.x) * xv.x; sumq = sumq + float(w.y) * xv.y; sumq = sumq + float(w.z) * xv.z; sumq = sumq + float(w.w) * xv.w; } acc = acc + d * sumq; } float s = metal::simd_sum(acc); if (lane == 0u) y[r] = (bflag != 0u) ? (s + bias[r]) : s; } ")

    (defn dth-q40-lane2-msl ()
        "kernel void form_q40_matvec_lane2_f32 (device const uchar* qb [[buffer(0)]], device const float* x [[buffer(1)]], device float* y [[buffer(2)]], device const float* bias [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& rows [[buffer(4)]], constant uint& cols [[buffer(5)]], constant uint& bflag [[buffer(6)]], uint gid [[thread_position_in_grid]], uint lane [[thread_index_in_simdgroup]]) { uint r = gid / 32u; if (r >= rows) return; uint nb = cols / 32u; ulong rowbase = (ulong)r * (ulong)nb * 18ul; float acc = 0.0f; for (uint b = lane; b < nb; b += 32u) { device const uchar* bp = qb + rowbase + (ulong)b * 18ul; ushort h = (ushort)bp[0] | ((ushort)bp[1] << 8); float d = float(as_type<half>(h)); device const uchar* qs = bp + 2u; device const float* xb = x + b * 32u; float sumq = 0.0f; for (uint i = 0u; i < 16u; i += 4u) { uchar4 w = uchar4(*(device const packed_uchar4*)(qs + i)); float4 xv = float4(*(device const packed_float4*)(xb + i)); sumq = sumq + float(int(w.x & 15u) - 8) * xv.x; sumq = sumq + float(int(w.y & 15u) - 8) * xv.y; sumq = sumq + float(int(w.z & 15u) - 8) * xv.z; sumq = sumq + float(int(w.w & 15u) - 8) * xv.w; } for (uint i = 0u; i < 16u; i += 4u) { uchar4 w = uchar4(*(device const packed_uchar4*)(qs + i)); float4 xv = float4(*(device const packed_float4*)(xb + 16u + i)); sumq = sumq + float(int(w.x >> 4u) - 8) * xv.x; sumq = sumq + float(int(w.y >> 4u) - 8) * xv.y; sumq = sumq + float(int(w.z >> 4u) - 8) * xv.z; sumq = sumq + float(int(w.w >> 4u) - 8) * xv.w; } acc = acc + d * sumq; } float s = metal::simd_sum(acc); if (lane == 0u) y[r] = (bflag != 0u) ? (s + bias[r]) : s; } ")

    (defn dth-q50-lane2-msl ()
        "kernel void form_q50_matvec_lane2_f32 (device const uchar* qb [[buffer(0)]], device const float* x [[buffer(1)]], device float* y [[buffer(2)]], device const float* bias [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& rows [[buffer(4)]], constant uint& cols [[buffer(5)]], constant uint& bflag [[buffer(6)]], uint gid [[thread_position_in_grid]], uint lane [[thread_index_in_simdgroup]]) { uint r = gid / 32u; if (r >= rows) return; uint nb = cols / 32u; ulong rowbase = (ulong)r * (ulong)nb * 22ul; float acc = 0.0f; for (uint b = lane; b < nb; b += 32u) { device const uchar* bp = qb + rowbase + (ulong)b * 22ul; ushort h = (ushort)bp[0] | ((ushort)bp[1] << 8); float d = float(as_type<half>(h)); uint qh = uint(bp[2]) | (uint(bp[3]) << 8u) | (uint(bp[4]) << 16u) | (uint(bp[5]) << 24u); device const uchar* qs = bp + 6u; device const float* xb = x + b * 32u; float sumq = 0.0f; for (uint i = 0u; i < 16u; i += 4u) { uchar4 w = uchar4(*(device const packed_uchar4*)(qs + i)); float4 xv = float4(*(device const packed_float4*)(xb + i)); sumq = sumq + float(int((w.x & 15u) | (((qh >> i) & 1u) << 4u)) - 16) * xv.x; sumq = sumq + float(int((w.y & 15u) | (((qh >> (i + 1u)) & 1u) << 4u)) - 16) * xv.y; sumq = sumq + float(int((w.z & 15u) | (((qh >> (i + 2u)) & 1u) << 4u)) - 16) * xv.z; sumq = sumq + float(int((w.w & 15u) | (((qh >> (i + 3u)) & 1u) << 4u)) - 16) * xv.w; } for (uint i = 0u; i < 16u; i += 4u) { uint ii = i + 16u; uchar4 w = uchar4(*(device const packed_uchar4*)(qs + i)); float4 xv = float4(*(device const packed_float4*)(xb + ii)); sumq = sumq + float(int((w.x >> 4u) | (((qh >> ii) & 1u) << 4u)) - 16) * xv.x; sumq = sumq + float(int((w.y >> 4u) | (((qh >> (ii + 1u)) & 1u) << 4u)) - 16) * xv.y; sumq = sumq + float(int((w.z >> 4u) | (((qh >> (ii + 2u)) & 1u) << 4u)) - 16) * xv.z; sumq = sumq + float(int((w.w >> 4u) | (((qh >> (ii + 3u)) & 1u) << 4u)) - 16) * xv.w; } acc = acc + d * sumq; } float s = metal::simd_sum(acc); if (lane == 0u) y[r] = (bflag != 0u) ? (s + bias[r]) : s; } ")

    (defn dth-q6k-lane2-msl ()
        "kernel void form_q6k_matvec_lane2_f32 (device const uchar* qb [[buffer(0)]], device const float* x [[buffer(1)]], device float* y [[buffer(2)]], device const float* bias [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& rows [[buffer(4)]], constant uint& cols [[buffer(5)]], constant uint& bflag [[buffer(6)]], uint gid [[thread_position_in_grid]], uint lane [[thread_index_in_simdgroup]]) { uint r = gid / 32u; if (r >= rows) return; uint ng = cols / 16u; ulong rowbase = (ulong)r * (ulong)(cols / 256u) * 210ul; float acc = 0.0f; for (uint g = lane; g < ng; g += 32u) { uint blk = g >> 4u; uint gi = g & 15u; device const uchar* b = qb + rowbase + (ulong)blk * 210ul; uint hh = gi >> 3u; uint rem = gi & 7u; uint gp = rem >> 1u; uint is = rem & 1u; ushort hd = (ushort)b[208] | ((ushort)b[209] << 8); float d = float(as_type<half>(hd)); int sci = int(b[192u + hh * 8u + is + 2u * gp]); int sc = sci < 128 ? sci : sci - 256; device const uchar* ql = b + hh * 64u + is * 16u + (gp & 1u) * 32u; device const uchar* qh = b + 128u + hh * 32u + is * 16u; uint sh4 = (gp >> 1u) * 4u; uint sh2 = gp * 2u; device const float* xg = x + g * 16u; float sumq = 0.0f; for (uint t = 0u; t < 16u; t += 4u) { uchar4 lb = uchar4(*(device const packed_uchar4*)(ql + t)); uchar4 hb = uchar4(*(device const packed_uchar4*)(qh + t)); float4 xv = float4(*(device const packed_float4*)(xg + t)); sumq = sumq + float(int(((lb.x >> sh4) & 15u) + ((hb.x >> sh2) & 3u) * 16u) - 32) * xv.x; sumq = sumq + float(int(((lb.y >> sh4) & 15u) + ((hb.y >> sh2) & 3u) * 16u) - 32) * xv.y; sumq = sumq + float(int(((lb.z >> sh4) & 15u) + ((hb.z >> sh2) & 3u) * 16u) - 32) * xv.z; sumq = sumq + float(int(((lb.w >> sh4) & 15u) + ((hb.w >> sh2) & 3u) * 16u) - 32) * xv.w; } acc = acc + (d * float(sc)) * sumq; } float s = metal::simd_sum(acc); if (lane == 0u) y[r] = (bflag != 0u) ? (s + bias[r]) : s; } ")

    (defn dth-q4k-lane2-msl ()
        "kernel void form_q4k_matvec_lane2_f32 (device const uchar* qb [[buffer(0)]], device const float* x [[buffer(1)]], device float* y [[buffer(2)]], device const float* bias [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& rows [[buffer(4)]], constant uint& cols [[buffer(5)]], constant uint& bflag [[buffer(6)]], uint gid [[thread_position_in_grid]], uint lane [[thread_index_in_simdgroup]]) { uint r = gid / 32u; if (r >= rows) return; uint ns = cols / 32u; ulong rowbase = (ulong)r * (ulong)(cols / 256u) * 144ul; float acc = 0.0f; for (uint sb = lane; sb < ns; sb += 32u) { uint blk = sb >> 3u; uint j = sb & 7u; device const uchar* b = qb + rowbase + (ulong)blk * 144ul; ushort hd = (ushort)b[0] | ((ushort)b[1] << 8); ushort hm = (ushort)b[2] | ((ushort)b[3] << 8); float d = float(as_type<half>(hd)); float dmin = float(as_type<half>(hm)); uint sc; uint mn; if (j < 4u) { sc = uint(b[4u + j]) & 63u; mn = uint(b[8u + j]) & 63u; } else { sc = (uint(b[8u + j]) & 15u) | ((uint(b[j]) >> 6u) << 4u); mn = (uint(b[8u + j]) >> 4u) | ((uint(b[4u + j]) >> 6u) << 4u); } float ds = d * float(sc); float dm = dmin * float(mn); uint c = j >> 1u; uint sh = (j & 1u) * 4u; device const uchar* qs = b + 16u + c * 32u; device const float* xg = x + sb * 32u; float sumq = 0.0f; float sumx = 0.0f; for (uint t = 0u; t < 32u; t += 4u) { uchar4 w = uchar4(*(device const packed_uchar4*)(qs + t)); float4 xv = float4(*(device const packed_float4*)(xg + t)); sumq = sumq + float((w.x >> sh) & 15u) * xv.x; sumx = sumx + xv.x; sumq = sumq + float((w.y >> sh) & 15u) * xv.y; sumx = sumx + xv.y; sumq = sumq + float((w.z >> sh) & 15u) * xv.z; sumx = sumx + xv.z; sumq = sumq + float((w.w >> sh) & 15u) * xv.w; sumx = sumx + xv.w; } acc = acc + (ds * sumq - dm * sumx); } float s = metal::simd_sum(acc); if (lane == 0u) y[r] = (bflag != 0u) ? (s + bias[r]) : s; } ")

    (defn dth-q5k-lane2-msl ()
        "kernel void form_q5k_matvec_lane2_f32 (device const uchar* qb [[buffer(0)]], device const float* x [[buffer(1)]], device float* y [[buffer(2)]], device const float* bias [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& rows [[buffer(4)]], constant uint& cols [[buffer(5)]], constant uint& bflag [[buffer(6)]], uint gid [[thread_position_in_grid]], uint lane [[thread_index_in_simdgroup]]) { uint r = gid / 32u; if (r >= rows) return; uint ns = cols / 32u; ulong rowbase = (ulong)r * (ulong)(cols / 256u) * 176ul; float acc = 0.0f; for (uint sb = lane; sb < ns; sb += 32u) { uint blk = sb >> 3u; uint j = sb & 7u; device const uchar* b = qb + rowbase + (ulong)blk * 176ul; ushort hd = (ushort)b[0] | ((ushort)b[1] << 8); ushort hm = (ushort)b[2] | ((ushort)b[3] << 8); float d = float(as_type<half>(hd)); float dmin = float(as_type<half>(hm)); uint sc; uint mn; if (j < 4u) { sc = uint(b[4u + j]) & 63u; mn = uint(b[8u + j]) & 63u; } else { sc = (uint(b[8u + j]) & 15u) | ((uint(b[j]) >> 6u) << 4u); mn = (uint(b[8u + j]) >> 4u) | ((uint(b[4u + j]) >> 6u) << 4u); } float ds = d * float(sc); float dm = dmin * float(mn); uint c = j >> 1u; uint sh = (j & 1u) * 4u; device const uchar* qs = b + 48u + c * 32u; device const uchar* qh = b + 16u; device const float* xg = x + sb * 32u; float sumq = 0.0f; float sumx = 0.0f; for (uint t = 0u; t < 32u; t += 4u) { uchar4 w = uchar4(*(device const packed_uchar4*)(qs + t)); uchar4 hb = uchar4(*(device const packed_uchar4*)(qh + t)); float4 xv = float4(*(device const packed_float4*)(xg + t)); sumq = sumq + float(((w.x >> sh) & 15u) | (((hb.x >> j) & 1u) << 4u)) * xv.x; sumx = sumx + xv.x; sumq = sumq + float(((w.y >> sh) & 15u) | (((hb.y >> j) & 1u) << 4u)) * xv.y; sumx = sumx + xv.y; sumq = sumq + float(((w.z >> sh) & 15u) | (((hb.z >> j) & 1u) << 4u)) * xv.z; sumx = sumx + xv.z; sumq = sumq + float(((w.w >> sh) & 15u) | (((hb.w >> j) & 1u) << 4u)) * xv.w; sumx = sumx + xv.w; } acc = acc + (ds * sumq - dm * sumx); } float s = metal::simd_sum(acc); if (lane == 0u) y[r] = (bflag != 0u) ? (s + bias[r]) : s; } ")

    ; ---- the TILED cooperative RMSNorm (2026-08-08, round two). form_rmsnorm_tg_f32's radius is
    ; a COMPILE-TIME 4096-float scratch, so d=5120 (qwen2-32B) and d=8192 (72B) stayed on the
    ; one-thread attestant — 129 serial norms a token on the 32B, each paying full device latency
    ; 2n times. This kernel removes the radius WITHOUT touching the order: squares are staged into
    ; the same 4096-float scratch one TILE at a time, thread 0 folds each tile ASCENDING into the
    ; same running sum (j = 0, 1, ... n-1, exactly the attestant's fold), Newton-50 unchanged, the
    ; elementwise normalize spread over the group. BIT FOR BIT the attestant at ANY n; must be
    ; dispatched as EXACTLY ONE threadgroup (mode 1).
    (defn dth-rms2-msl ()
        "kernel void form_rmsnorm_tg2_f32 (device const float* x [[buffer(0)]], device const float* g [[buffer(1)]], device float* y [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& n [[buffer(3)]], constant float& eps [[buffer(4)]], uint t [[thread_position_in_threadgroup]], uint nt [[threads_per_threadgroup]]) { threadgroup float sq[4096]; threadgroup float sinv[1]; float ss = 0.0f; uint base = 0u; while (base < n) { uint m = n - base; if (m > 4096u) m = 4096u; uint j = t; while (j < m) { float xv = x[base + j]; sq[j] = xv * xv; j += nt; } metal::threadgroup_barrier(metal::mem_flags::mem_threadgroup); if (t == 0u) { uint k = 0u; while (k < m) { ss = ss + sq[k]; k += 1u; } } metal::threadgroup_barrier(metal::mem_flags::mem_threadgroup); base += 4096u; } if (t == 0u) { float meansq = ss / float(n); float sdv = meansq + eps; float gg = sdv; uint it = 50u; while (it > 0u) { it -= 1u; gg = 0.5f * (gg + sdv / gg); } sinv[0] = 1.0f / gg; } metal::threadgroup_barrier(metal::mem_flags::mem_threadgroup); float inv = sinv[0]; uint j = t; while (j < n) { float nm = x[j] * inv; y[j] = nm * g[j]; j += nt; } } ")

    ; ---- attention in THREE dispatches (2026-08-08, round two), and every fold keeps its
    ; element's association. form_gqa_decode_f32 gives one thread a whole head: at the 32B shape
    ; that is 40 threads serially walking the cache — measured 394 us per dispatch (stage-probe.fk),
    ; ~25 ms of a 64-layer token. The three pieces are maps over independent elements:
    ;   scores: thread (h,t) computes score(h,t) — the dot's c-descending fold UNCHANGED per score
    ;   soft:   thread h does the attestant's max/exp/normalize middle verbatim (serial per head)
    ;   out:    thread (h,i) folds t ASCENDING for output element i — the attestant's own t-then-i
    ;           nesting reads element-wise as exactly this fold, value for value
    ; BIT FOR BIT the one-dispatch attestant, which stays in the unit.
    (defn dth-attn-scores-msl ()
        "kernel void form_gqa_scores_f32 (device const float* q [[buffer(0)]], device const float* kc [[buffer(1)]], device float* sc [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& npos [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& nq [[buffer(4)]], constant uint& nkv [[buffer(5)]], constant uint& hd [[buffer(6)]], constant float& scale [[buffer(7)]], constant uint& sstride [[buffer(8)]], uint gid [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (gid >= nq * npos) return; uint h = gid / npos; uint t = gid - h * npos; uint grp = nq / nkv; uint kvh = h / grp; uint KVD = nkv * hd; uint qoff = h * hd; uint koff = kvh * hd; uint S = h * sstride; float acc = 0.0f; uint c = hd; while (c > 0) { c -= 1; float p = q[qoff + c] * kc[t * KVD + koff + c]; acc = p + acc; } sc[S + t] = acc * scale; } ")

    (defn dth-attn-soft-msl ()
        "kernel void form_gqa_soft_f32 (device float* sc [[buffer(0)]], constant uint& npos [[buffer(1)]], constant uint& nq [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& sstride [[buffer(3)]], uint h [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (h >= nq) return; uint S = h * sstride; uint E = (nq + h) * sstride; float mx = sc[S + 0]; uint t = 1; while (t < npos) { if (sc[S + t] > mx) { mx = sc[S + t]; } t += 1; } float sumes = 0.0f; t = 0; while (t < npos) { float e = fexp(sc[S + t] - mx); sc[E + t] = e; sumes = sumes + e; t += 1; } float invs = 1.0f / sumes; t = 0; while (t < npos) { sc[S + t] = sc[E + t] * invs; t += 1; } } ")

    (defn dth-attn-out-msl ()
        "kernel void form_gqa_out_f32 (device const float* vc [[buffer(0)]], device const float* sc [[buffer(1)]], device float* y [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& npos [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& nq [[buffer(4)]], constant uint& nkv [[buffer(5)]], constant uint& hd [[buffer(6)]], constant uint& sstride [[buffer(7)]], uint gid [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (gid >= nq * hd) return; uint h = gid / hd; uint i = gid - h * hd; uint grp = nq / nkv; uint kvh = h / grp; uint KVD = nkv * hd; uint S = h * sstride; uint koff = kvh * hd; float acc = 0.0f; uint t = 0; while (t < npos) { float pv = vc[t * KVD + koff + i] * sc[S + t]; acc = acc + pv; t += 1; } y[h * hd + i] = acc; } ")

    ; ---- the WIDE RMSNorm (2026-08-08, round two) — the norm takes the lane fold's standing.
    ; The bit-exact tiled twin above measured 316 us at d=5120 (layer-probe.fk, fenced): the
    ; ascending sum is ONE thread's dependent chain and cannot go wider without reassociating.
    ; At 129 norms a token that was 41 ms of the 32B's 109 — the largest single term. This twin
    ; REASSOCIATES the sum of squares: thread t folds x[t], x[t+256], ... ascending (chain depth
    ; ceil(n/256)), metal::simd_sum per simdgroup, thread 0 folds the 8 partials ascending.
    ; The terms are all NONNEGATIVE, so there is no cancellation and the bound is plain:
    ; |ss_wide - ss*| <= (ceil(n/256) + 32 + 8) * 2^-24 * ss — relative ~2e-6 at n=8192 — and it
    ; carries into 1/rms as the same relative order, the same magnitude the lane matvec's named
    ; epsilon already admits per element. Newton-50 and the normalize are UNCHANGED. The
    ; bit-exact twins (serial + tiled) stay in the unit; the gate is the measured stream.
    (defn dth-rms-wide-msl ()
        "kernel void form_rmsnorm_wide_f32 (device const float* x [[buffer(0)]], device const float* g [[buffer(1)]], device float* y [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& n [[buffer(3)]], constant float& eps [[buffer(4)]], uint t [[thread_position_in_threadgroup]], uint nt [[threads_per_threadgroup]], uint lane [[thread_index_in_simdgroup]], uint sg [[simdgroup_index_in_threadgroup]]) { threadgroup float part[32]; threadgroup float sinv[1]; float a = 0.0f; uint j = t; while (j < n) { float xv = x[j]; a = a + xv * xv; j += nt; } float sa = metal::simd_sum(a); if (lane == 0u) part[sg] = sa; metal::threadgroup_barrier(metal::mem_flags::mem_threadgroup); if (t == 0u) { uint nsg = (nt + 31u) / 32u; float ss = 0.0f; uint k = 0u; while (k < nsg) { ss = ss + part[k]; k += 1u; } float meansq = ss / float(n); float sdv = meansq + eps; float gg = sdv; uint it = 50u; while (it > 0u) { it -= 1u; gg = 0.5f * (gg + sdv / gg); } sinv[0] = 1.0f / gg; } metal::threadgroup_barrier(metal::mem_flags::mem_threadgroup); float inv = sinv[0]; j = t; while (j < n) { float nm = x[j] * inv; y[j] = nm * g[j]; j += nt; } } ")

    ; ---- the WIDE LayerNorm (2026-08-09, round two) — phi2's norm takes the same standing the
    ; RMSNorm just did. The serial attestant (dth-ln-msl) is one thread over 3n device reads;
    ; this twin reassociates BOTH folds: thread t sums x[t], x[t+256], ... ascending, simd_sum,
    ; thread 0 folds 8 partials ascending -> mean; the same shape again over (x-mean)^2 -> var.
    ; The mean's terms are SIGNED, so its bound anchors to the magnitude sum:
    ; |m_wide - m*| <= (ceil(n/256)+40) * 2^-24 * SUM|x_j| / n; the variance terms are
    ; nonnegative and bound as the RMSNorm's. Newton-50 and the normalize are the attestant's
    ; own lines. The serial attestant stays in the unit; the gate is the measured stream.
    (defn dth-ln-wide-msl ()
        "kernel void form_layernorm_wide_f32 (device const float* x [[buffer(0)]], device const float* g [[buffer(1)]], device const float* bb [[buffer(2)]], device float* y [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& n [[buffer(4)]], constant float& eps [[buffer(5)]], uint t [[thread_position_in_threadgroup]], uint nt [[threads_per_threadgroup]], uint lane [[thread_index_in_simdgroup]], uint sg [[simdgroup_index_in_threadgroup]]) { threadgroup float part[32]; threadgroup float sh2[2]; float a = 0.0f; uint j = t; while (j < n) { a = a + x[j]; j += nt; } float saa = metal::simd_sum(a); if (lane == 0u) part[sg] = saa; metal::threadgroup_barrier(metal::mem_flags::mem_threadgroup); if (t == 0u) { uint nsg = (nt + 31u) / 32u; float s = 0.0f; uint k = 0u; while (k < nsg) { s = s + part[k]; k += 1u; } sh2[0] = s / float(n); } metal::threadgroup_barrier(metal::mem_flags::mem_threadgroup); float mean = sh2[0]; float v = 0.0f; j = t; while (j < n) { float c = x[j] - mean; v = v + c * c; j += nt; } float sv = metal::simd_sum(v); metal::threadgroup_barrier(metal::mem_flags::mem_threadgroup); if (lane == 0u) part[sg] = sv; metal::threadgroup_barrier(metal::mem_flags::mem_threadgroup); if (t == 0u) { uint nsg = (nt + 31u) / 32u; float s = 0.0f; uint k = 0u; while (k < nsg) { s = s + part[k]; k += 1u; } float sdv = s / float(n) + eps; float gg = sdv; uint it = 50u; while (it > 0u) { it -= 1u; gg = 0.5f * (gg + sdv / gg); } sh2[1] = 1.0f / gg; } metal::threadgroup_barrier(metal::mem_flags::mem_threadgroup); float inv = sh2[1]; j = t; while (j < n) { y[j] = ((x[j] - mean) * inv) * g[j] + bb[j]; j += nt; } } ")

    ; ---- the FUSED residual+norm (2026-08-09, round three). Round two's wall decomposition
    ; said the remaining gap is STAGES, not bytes: ~13.7 us of fenced-stage quantum per stage,
    ; 13-15 stages a layer. Every block spent two of them on "add the residual" then "norm the
    ; sum" — two dispatches whose data dependency is total. This kernel is their composition in
    ; ONE dispatch: when addflag=1 the group first writes x[j] = x[j] + h[j] (each thread its
    ; own j's — the attestant add kernel's exact elementwise op, a bit-exact map), barriers on
    ; device memory, then runs form_rmsnorm_wide_f32's body UNCHANGED on the updated x. The
    ; fusion itself introduces NO new reassociation: the add is exact composition, the norm
    ; carries the wide twin's already-stated bound. addflag=0 skips the add (h unread) and IS
    ; the wide norm. ONE threadgroup, mode 1, like both parents.
    (defn dth-addrms-msl ()
        "kernel void form_add_rmsnorm_wide_f32 (device float* x [[buffer(0)]], device const float* h [[buffer(1)]], device const float* g [[buffer(2)]], device float* y [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& n [[buffer(4)]], constant float& eps [[buffer(5)]], constant uint& addflag [[buffer(6)]], uint t [[thread_position_in_threadgroup]], uint nt [[threads_per_threadgroup]], uint lane [[thread_index_in_simdgroup]], uint sg [[simdgroup_index_in_threadgroup]]) { threadgroup float part[32]; threadgroup float sinv[1]; if (addflag != 0u) { uint jj = t; while (jj < n) { x[jj] = x[jj] + h[jj]; jj += nt; } } metal::threadgroup_barrier(metal::mem_flags::mem_device); float a = 0.0f; uint j = t; while (j < n) { float xv = x[j]; a = a + xv * xv; j += nt; } float sa = metal::simd_sum(a); if (lane == 0u) part[sg] = sa; metal::threadgroup_barrier(metal::mem_flags::mem_threadgroup); if (t == 0u) { uint nsg = (nt + 31u) / 32u; float ss = 0.0f; uint k = 0u; while (k < nsg) { ss = ss + part[k]; k += 1u; } float meansq = ss / float(n); float sdv = meansq + eps; float gg = sdv; uint it = 50u; while (it > 0u) { it -= 1u; gg = 0.5f * (gg + sdv / gg); } sinv[0] = 1.0f / gg; } metal::threadgroup_barrier(metal::mem_flags::mem_threadgroup); float inv = sinv[0]; j = t; while (j < n) { float nm = x[j] * inv; y[j] = nm * g[j]; j += nt; } } ")

    ; The phi2 twin: the parallel-residual block ends with TWO adds — x = (x + attn) + ffn, in
    ; that association, the attestant's own two-dispatch order — then the next norm reads the
    ; sum. Fused the same way: both adds per element in one thread (same association, bit-exact
    ; map), device barrier, then form_layernorm_wide_f32's body unchanged (its stated bounds).
    (defn dth-add2ln-msl ()
        "kernel void form_add2_layernorm_wide_f32 (device float* x [[buffer(0)]], device const float* h1 [[buffer(1)]], device const float* h2 [[buffer(2)]], device const float* g [[buffer(3)]], device const float* bb [[buffer(4)]], device float* y [[buffer(5)]], constant uint& n [[buffer(6)]], constant float& eps [[buffer(7)]], constant uint& addflag [[buffer(8)]], uint t [[thread_position_in_threadgroup]], uint nt [[threads_per_threadgroup]], uint lane [[thread_index_in_simdgroup]], uint sg [[simdgroup_index_in_threadgroup]]) { threadgroup float part[32]; threadgroup float sh2[2]; if (addflag != 0u) { uint jj = t; while (jj < n) { x[jj] = (x[jj] + h1[jj]) + h2[jj]; jj += nt; } } metal::threadgroup_barrier(metal::mem_flags::mem_device); float a = 0.0f; uint j = t; while (j < n) { a = a + x[j]; j += nt; } float saa = metal::simd_sum(a); if (lane == 0u) part[sg] = saa; metal::threadgroup_barrier(metal::mem_flags::mem_threadgroup); if (t == 0u) { uint nsg = (nt + 31u) / 32u; float s = 0.0f; uint k = 0u; while (k < nsg) { s = s + part[k]; k += 1u; } sh2[0] = s / float(n); } metal::threadgroup_barrier(metal::mem_flags::mem_threadgroup); float mean = sh2[0]; float v = 0.0f; j = t; while (j < n) { float c = x[j] - mean; v = v + c * c; j += nt; } float sv = metal::simd_sum(v); metal::threadgroup_barrier(metal::mem_flags::mem_threadgroup); if (lane == 0u) part[sg] = sv; metal::threadgroup_barrier(metal::mem_flags::mem_threadgroup); if (t == 0u) { uint nsg = (nt + 31u) / 32u; float s = 0.0f; uint k = 0u; while (k < nsg) { s = s + part[k]; k += 1u; } float sdv = s / float(n) + eps; float gg = sdv; uint it = 50u; while (it > 0u) { it -= 1u; gg = 0.5f * (gg + sdv / gg); } sh2[1] = 1.0f / gg; } metal::threadgroup_barrier(metal::mem_flags::mem_threadgroup); float inv = sh2[1]; j = t; while (j < n) { y[j] = ((x[j] - mean) * inv) * g[j] + bb[j]; j += nt; } } ")

    ; ---- rope that STORES (2026-08-09, round three). The K rope rotated in place and a copy
    ; then moved the whole vector into the cache — a dispatch and a fenced stage whose only work
    ; was a shifted destination. These twins are the pair-grain rope kernels with d[doff+...]
    ; as the destination instead of v itself: identical arithmetic per pair, a bit-exact map
    ; (the ds4 reference keeps the ROTATION's arithmetic unfused for exactness; the same
    ; boundary is kept here — only the STORE moved). RADIUS: every element of the head must be
    ; a rotated pair, or the unrotated tail would never reach the cache — the neox form asks
    ; rd == hd and rd even, the adjacent form hd even; outside it the in-place rope + copy stay.
    (defn dth-neox-pair-store-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device const float* v [[buffer(0)]], device const float* fr [[buffer(1)]], device float* d [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& nh [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& hd [[buffer(4)]], constant uint& rd [[buffer(5)]], constant uint& pos [[buffer(6)]], constant float& base [[buffer(7)]], constant uint& doff [[buffer(8)]], uint gid [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { uint np = rd / 2u; if (gid >= nh * np) return; uint h = gid / np; uint j = gid - h * np; uint o = h * hd; float ex = (-2.0f * float(j)) / float(rd); float fq = fpow(base, ex) / fr[j]; float a = float(pos) * fq; float ca = fcos(a); float sa = fsin(a); float q0 = v[o + j]; float q1 = v[o + j + np]; float t0 = q0 * ca; float t1 = q1 * sa; d[doff + o + j] = t0 - t1; float t2 = q0 * sa; float t3 = q1 * ca; d[doff + o + j + np] = t2 + t3; }")))

    (defn dth-pair-store-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device const float* v [[buffer(0)]], device const float* fr [[buffer(1)]], device float* d [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& nh [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& hd [[buffer(4)]], constant uint& pos [[buffer(5)]], constant float& base [[buffer(6)]], constant uint& doff [[buffer(7)]], uint gid [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { uint np = hd / 2u; if (gid >= nh * np) return; uint h = gid / np; uint pr = gid - h * np; uint i = pr * 2u; uint o = h * hd; float ex = (-1.0f * float(i)) / float(hd); float fq = fpow(base, ex) / fr[i / 2u]; float a = float(pos) * fq; float ca = fcos(a); float sa = fsin(a); float q0 = v[o + i]; float q1 = v[o + i + 1u]; float t0 = q0 * ca; float t1 = q1 * sa; d[doff + o + i] = t0 - t1; float t2 = q0 * sa; float t3 = q1 * ca; d[doff + o + i + 1u] = t2 + t3; }")))

    ; The pragma is the carrier header's own stated fix: this door's default COMPILES CONTRACTED,
    ; and the cell owns every number, so the cell says so in the text it emits.
    (defn dth-msl ()
        (str_concat "#include <metal_stdlib>\n#pragma clang fp contract(off)\n"
        (str_concat (q6m-msl-unit "form_q6k_dequant_f32" "form_q6k_matvec_f32")
        (str_concat (q4m-msl-unit "form_q4k_dequant_f32" "form_q4k_matvec_f32")
        (str_concat (q80-msl-appendix "form_q80_dequant_f32" "form_q80_matvec_f32" "form_q80_matvec_lane_f32")
        (str_concat (q5m-msl-appendix "form_q5k_dequant_f32" "form_q5k_matvec_f32"
                                      "form_q50_dequant_f32" "form_q50_matvec_f32")
        (str_concat (ldm-msl-unit)
        (str_concat (dth-copy-msl "form_copy_off_f32")
        (str_concat (dth-neox-msl "form_rope_neox_f32")
        (str_concat (dth-ln-msl "form_layernorm_f32")
        (str_concat (dth-gelu-msl "form_gelu_f32")
        (str_concat (dth-copyfrom-msl "form_copy_from_f32")
        (str_concat (dth-q40-weight-msl)
        (str_concat (dth-q40-dequant-msl "form_q40_dequant_f32")
        (str_concat (dth-q40-matvec-msl "form_q40_matvec_f32")
        (str_concat (qml-msl-appendix)
        (str_concat (dth-q5k-lane-msl "form_q5k_matvec_lane_f32")
        (str_concat (dth-q50-lane-msl "form_q50_matvec_lane_f32")
        (str_concat (dth-q40-lane-msl "form_q40_matvec_lane_f32")
        (str_concat (dth-q80-lane2-msl)
        (str_concat (dth-q40-lane2-msl)
        (str_concat (dth-q50-lane2-msl)
        (str_concat (dth-q6k-lane2-msl)
        (str_concat (dth-q4k-lane2-msl)
        (str_concat (dth-q5k-lane2-msl)
        (str_concat (dth-rms2-msl)
        (str_concat (dth-attn-scores-msl)
        (str_concat (dth-attn-soft-msl)
        (str_concat (dth-attn-out-msl)
        (str_concat (dth-neox-pair-msl "form_rope_neox_pair_f32")
        (str_concat (dth-rms-wide-msl)
        (str_concat (dth-ln-wide-msl)
        (str_concat (dth-addrms-msl)
        (str_concat (dth-add2ln-msl)
        (str_concat (dth-neox-pair-store-msl "form_rope_neox_pair_store_f32")
                    (dth-pair-store-msl "form_rope_pair_store_f32"))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))

    ; ================= the file's numbers, in ONE walk =================
    (defn dth-header-window () 40000000)
    (defn dth-alignment () 32)
    (defn dth-src (path) (eqr-of-file path 0 (dth-header-window)))

    (defn dth-ti-name (src off) (substring src (add off 8) (add (add off 8) (egg-ti-namelen src off))))
    (defn dth-ti-dim1 (src off) (if (gt (egg-ti-ndims src off) 1) (egg-ti-dim src off 1) 1))

    ; bytes by ggml type: F32 0, F16 1, Q5_0 6, Q8_0 8, Q4_K 12, Q5_K 13, Q6_K 14. Anything else
    ; prices 0, and a zero-length view REFUSES at the door instead of mapping a wrong window.
    (defn dth-price (t n)
        (if (eq t 0) (mul n 4)
        (if (eq t 1) (mul n 2)
        (if (eq t 2) (mul (div n 32) 18)
        (if (eq t 6) (mul (div n 32) 22)
        (if (eq t 8) (mul (div n 32) 34)
        (if (eq t 12) (mul (div n 256) 144)
        (if (eq t 13) (mul (div n 256) 176)
        (if (eq t 14) (mul (div n 256) 210) 0)))))))))

    ; One row: (name type d0 d1 dataoff bytes). One walk builds every row.
    (defn dth-table-row (src off)
        (do (let t (egg-ti-type src off))
            (let d0 (egg-ti-dim0 src off))
            (let d1 (dth-ti-dim1 src off))
            (list (dth-ti-name src off) t d0 d1 (egg-ti-dataoff src off) (dth-price t (mul d0 d1)))))

    (defn dth-table-walk (src off n acc)
        (if (le n 0) acc
            (dth-table-walk src (egg-ti-next src off) (sub n 1)
                (append acc (list (dth-table-row src off))))))

    (defn dth-table (src)
        (dth-table-walk src (egg-tinfo-start src) (egg-tensor-count src) (empty)))

    (defn dth-row-find (tab name)
        (if (eq (len tab) 0) 0
            (if (str_eq (nth (head tab) 0) name) (head tab) (dth-row-find (tail tab) name))))

    ; A tensor VIEW from a table row: (handle rows cols type). rows = dim1, cols = dim0.
    (defn dth-tv (tab base path name)
        (do (let r (dth-row-find tab name))
            (if (eq r 0) (list 0 0 0 (sub 0 1))
                (list (metal_buf_from_file path (add base (nth r 4)) (nth r 5))
                      (nth r 3) (nth r 2) (nth r 1)))))

    (defn dth-tv-h  (t) (nth t 0))
    (defn dth-tv-r  (t) (nth t 1))
    (defn dth-tv-c  (t) (nth t 2))
    (defn dth-tv-ty (t) (nth t 3))
    (defn dth-tv-none? (t) (eq (dth-tv-ty t) (sub 0 1)))

    (defn dth-blk (l suffix) (str_concat "blk." (str_concat (int_to_str l) (str_concat "." suffix))))

    ; Twelve entries per layer: the nine every dense block has, then the three biases a qwen2 block
    ; adds — ABSENT is a fact about the table and dispatches nothing.
    (defn dth-layer (tab base path l)
        (list (dth-tv tab base path (dth-blk l "attn_norm.weight"))
              (dth-tv tab base path (dth-blk l "attn_q.weight"))
              (dth-tv tab base path (dth-blk l "attn_k.weight"))
              (dth-tv tab base path (dth-blk l "attn_v.weight"))
              (dth-tv tab base path (dth-blk l "attn_output.weight"))
              (dth-tv tab base path (dth-blk l "ffn_norm.weight"))
              (dth-tv tab base path (dth-blk l "ffn_gate.weight"))
              (dth-tv tab base path (dth-blk l "ffn_up.weight"))
              (dth-tv tab base path (dth-blk l "ffn_down.weight"))
              (dth-tv tab base path (dth-blk l "attn_q.bias"))
              (dth-tv tab base path (dth-blk l "attn_k.bias"))
              (dth-tv tab base path (dth-blk l "attn_v.bias"))))

    (defn dth-layers (tab base path l n acc)
        (if (ge l n) acc
            (dth-layers tab base path (add l 1) n (append acc (list (dth-layer tab base path l))))))

    (defn dth-out-tv (tab base path)
        (do (let r (dth-row-find tab "output.weight"))
            (if (eq r 0) (dth-tv tab base path "token_embd.weight")
                (dth-tv tab base path "output.weight"))))

    ; ================= metadata by arch prefix =================
    (defn dth-key (arch suffix) (str_concat arch (str_concat "." suffix)))

    ; A BOOL KV is type 7, one byte. gmt-u32 refuses it; this reads it as what it is.
    (defn dth-bool (src key dflt)
        (do (let off (gmt-find src key))
            (if (eq off (gmt-absent)) dflt
                (if (eq (gmt-vtype src off) 7) (eqr-at src (gmt-valoff src off)) dflt))))

    (defn dth-u32-or (src key dflt)
        (do (let v (gmt-u32 src key))
            (if (eq v (gmt-absent)) dflt v)))

    ; ================= the pool =================
    ; pipes: 0 q6mv 1 q4mv 2 q80mv 3 q6dq 4 q4dq 5 q80dq 6 rms 7 rope 8 neox 9 attn 10 swiglu
    ;        11 add 12 argmax 13 copy 14 q5kmv 15 q5kdq 16 q50mv 17 q50dq 18 q40mv 19 q40dq
    ;        20 layernorm 21 gelu 22 copyfrom
    ;        23 rmsnorm_tg 24 argmax_part 25 argmax_comb 26 rope_pair   (the bit-exact twins,
    ;        adopted 2026-08-08 from the llama lane where each carries its stated radius)
    ;        27 q6lane 28 q4lane 29 q80lane 30 q5klane 31 q50lane 32 q40lane   (the SIMD-group
    ;        matvecs — one group per row, the one reassociation is simd_sum, epsilon named above)
    ;        33 q6lane2 34 q4klane2 35 q80lane2 36 q5klane2 37 q50lane2 38 q40lane2   (the
    ;        FACTORED-SCALE lane matvecs, 2026-08-08 round two — scale once per group, bitmask
    ;        decode, bounds in the kernel block above; these are the dispatched ones, and since
    ;        2026-08-09 round three each carries the bit-exact bias epilogue)
    ;        46 add_rmsnorm_wide 47 add2_layernorm_wide 48 rope_neox_pair_store
    ;        49 rope_pair_store   (round three's stage fusions — residual+norm in one dispatch,
    ;        K rope stored straight into its cache row; bounds at their kernels)
    (defn dth-pipes (msl)
        (list (metal_pipeline msl "form_q6k_matvec_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q4k_matvec_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q80_matvec_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q6k_dequant_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q4k_dequant_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q80_dequant_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_rmsnorm_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_rope_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_rope_neox_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_gqa_decode_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_swiglu_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_add_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_argmax_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_copy_off_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q5k_matvec_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q5k_dequant_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q50_matvec_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q50_dequant_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q40_matvec_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q40_dequant_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_layernorm_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_gelu_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_copy_from_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_rmsnorm_tg_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_argmax_part_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_argmax_comb_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_rope_pair_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q6k_matvec_lane_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q4k_matvec_lane_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q80_matvec_lane_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q5k_matvec_lane_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q50_matvec_lane_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q40_matvec_lane_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q6k_matvec_lane2_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q4k_matvec_lane2_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q80_matvec_lane2_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q5k_matvec_lane2_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q50_matvec_lane2_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q40_matvec_lane2_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_rmsnorm_tg2_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_gqa_scores_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_gqa_soft_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_gqa_out_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_rope_neox_pair_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_rmsnorm_wide_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_layernorm_wide_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_add_rmsnorm_wide_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_add2_layernorm_wide_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_rope_neox_pair_store_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_rope_pair_store_f32")))

    (defn dth-pipe-ok? (ps) (if (eq (len ps) 0) true (if (eq (head ps) 0) false (dth-pipe-ok? (tail ps)))))

    ; bufs: 0 X 1 Xb 2 Q 3 Ks 4 Vs 5 Attn 6 Proj 7 Ffn 8 Gate 9 Up 10 Act 11 Logits 12 Scratch
    ;       13 OutI 14 OutV 15 PartI 16 PartV (the two-stage argmax partials, 1024 entries)
    ; Q, Attn are sized qOut = nHead * headDim, which is NOT dModel on every file (nanbeige: 6144
    ; over d=3072; MiniCPM5: 2048 over 1536).
    (defn dth-bufs (dModel dFF qOut kvd vocabN nHead maxpos)
        (list (metal_buf_alloc (mul dModel 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul dModel 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul qOut 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul kvd 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul kvd 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul qOut 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul dModel 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul dModel 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul dFF 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul dFF 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul dFF 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul vocabN 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul (mul 2 nHead) maxpos) 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc 16)
              (metal_buf_alloc 16)
              (metal_buf_alloc 4096)
              (metal_buf_alloc 4096)))

    ; nLayer * nLoop cache banks: pass 2 must never read pass 1's history as its own.
    (defn dth-cache (n kvd maxpos acc)
        (if (le n 0) acc
            (dth-cache (sub n 1) kvd maxpos
                (append acc (list (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul kvd maxpos) 4)))))))

    ; rope freqs: the file's own rope_freqs.weight, or np words of 1.0f this cell WRITES.
    (defn dth-ones (n acc) (if (le n 0) acc (dth-ones (sub n 1) (str_concat acc (md-le32 1065353216)))))
    (defn dth-rope-freqs (tab base path np)
        (do (let r (dth-row-find tab "rope_freqs.weight"))
            (if (eq r 0)
                (do (let h (metal_buf_alloc (mul np 4)))
                    (metal_buf_write h 0 (dth-ones np ""))
                    h)
                (dth-tv-h (dth-tv tab base path "rope_freqs.weight")))))

    ; ================= dispatches =================
    ; EVERY MODE-0 DISPATCH CAPS ITS GROUP AT 256 and EVERY BATCH IS CONCURRENT with hazards
    ; DECLARED BY THIS CELL via barrier_before — the llama lane's own proven shape (2026-08-04:
    ; 1083 ms/token at the 1024 ceiling against 388 at 256; serial -> concurrent was the twins'
    ; 3x), adopted here 2026-08-08. bb on each helper is exactly "must I see my predecessors'
    ; writes": independent runs (q/k/v off one normed vector, gate/up, the two ropes, the two
    ; cache copies) share a stage, everything else fences.
    ; every matvec is a LANE matvec (one SIMD group of 32 per row, grid = rows * 32): the serial
    ; attestants stay in the unit and the band's CPU twins still answer to them; the lane twins
    ; answer to the named epsilon and to the measured stream gate.
    ; the bias rides the matvec's own epilogue (round three): a present bias binds at slot 3
    ; with bflag=1 — the same one f32 add the attestant's separate dispatch performed, fused
    ; bit-exactly; an absent bias binds y itself (unread) with bflag=0 and the store is s
    ; exactly as before.
    (defn dth-mv-pipe (ps tv)
        (if (eq (dth-tv-ty tv) 14) (nth ps 33)
        (if (eq (dth-tv-ty tv) 12) (nth ps 34)
        (if (eq (dth-tv-ty tv) 13) (nth ps 36)
        (if (eq (dth-tv-ty tv) 6) (nth ps 37)
        (if (eq (dth-tv-ty tv) 2) (nth ps 38) (nth ps 35)))))))

    (defn dth-mvb (ps tv xh yh bh bf bb)
        (metal_enqueue (dth-mv-pipe ps tv)
                       (md-bind16 (list (dth-tv-h tv) xh yh bh)
                                  (list (dth-tv-r tv) (dth-tv-c tv) bf) 256 0 0 bb)
                       (mul (dth-tv-r tv) 32)))

    (defn dth-mv (ps tv xh yh bb) (dth-mvb ps tv xh yh yh 0 bb))

    (defn dth-mvbias (ps tv xh yh btv bb)
        (if (dth-tv-none? btv) (dth-mv ps tv xh yh bb)
            (dth-mvb ps tv xh yh (dth-tv-h btv) 1 bb)))

    (defn dth-dq (ps tv yh off n bb)
        (metal_enqueue (if (eq (dth-tv-ty tv) 14) (nth ps 3)
                       (if (eq (dth-tv-ty tv) 12) (nth ps 4)
                       (if (eq (dth-tv-ty tv) 13) (nth ps 15)
                       (if (eq (dth-tv-ty tv) 6) (nth ps 17)
                       (if (eq (dth-tv-ty tv) 2) (nth ps 19) (nth ps 5))))))
                       (md-bind16 (list (dth-tv-h tv) yh) (list off n) 256 0 0 bb)
                       n))

    ; the WIDE RMSNorm (pipe 44) dispatches: reassociated sum of squares under the nonnegative
    ; bound stated at its kernel, gated by the measured stream. The bit-exact twins — the serial
    ; attestant (pipe 6) and the tiled cooperative form (pipe 39, any n) — stay in the unit and
    ; the CPU twins still answer to them. ONE threadgroup, honored by mode 1.
    (defn dth-rms (ps xh gtv yh n epsBits bb)
        (metal_enqueue (nth ps 44) (md-bind16 (list xh (dth-tv-h gtv) yh) (list n epsBits)
                                              256 0 1 bb) 1))

    ; residual + norm as ONE stage (pipe 46): ph is the pending residual handle, 0 when the
    ; entry has none (first block of a pass — x is the embedding or a freshly normed pass
    ; boundary). ph=0 binds x itself unread and IS the wide norm, dispatch for dispatch.
    (defn dth-addrms (ps xh ph gtv yh n epsBits bb)
        (metal_enqueue (nth ps 46)
                       (md-bind16 (list xh (if (eq ph 0) xh ph) (dth-tv-h gtv) yh)
                                  (list n epsBits (if (eq ph 0) 0 1)) 256 0 1 bb) 1))

    ; style 0: adjacent pairs over the whole head — at PAIR grain (a thread map, not an order;
    ; radius: hd even, else the per-head attestant). style 1: half-split over the first rd dims.
    (defn dth-rope (ps style vh ropeH nh hd rd pos baseBits bb)
        (if (eq style 1)
            (if (eq (mod rd 2) 0)
                (metal_enqueue (nth ps 43) (md-bind16 (list vh ropeH) (list nh hd rd pos baseBits)
                                                      256 0 0 bb) (mul nh (div rd 2)))
                (metal_enqueue (nth ps 8) (md-bind16 (list vh ropeH) (list nh hd rd pos baseBits)
                                                     256 0 0 bb) nh))
            (if (eq (mod hd 2) 0)
                (metal_enqueue (nth ps 26) (md-bind16 (list vh ropeH) (list nh hd pos baseBits)
                                                      256 0 0 bb) (mul nh (div hd 2)))
                (metal_enqueue (nth ps 7) (md-bind16 (list vh ropeH) (list nh hd pos baseBits)
                                                     256 0 0 bb) nh))))

    ; rope that stores into the cache row (pipes 48/49): legal only when every element of the
    ; head is a rotated pair (neox: rd == hd and rd even; adjacent: hd even) — outside that
    ; radius an unrotated tail would never reach the cache, so the in-place rope + copy stay.
    (defn dth-ropestore-ok? (style hd rd)
        (if (eq style 1)
            (if (eq rd hd) (eq (mod rd 2) 0) false)
            (eq (mod hd 2) 0)))

    (defn dth-rope-store (ps style vh ropeH dh doff nh hd rd pos baseBits bb)
        (if (eq style 1)
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 48)
                           (md-bind16 (list vh ropeH dh) (list nh hd rd pos baseBits doff)
                                      256 0 0 bb) (mul nh (div rd 2)))
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 49)
                           (md-bind16 (list vh ropeH dh) (list nh hd pos baseBits doff)
                                      256 0 0 bb) (mul nh (div hd 2)))))

    ; the K/V path to the cache in ONE stage beside rope-q: K rope-stores straight into its
    ; cache row (bit-exact map, destination shifted), V is the plain copy — all three
    ; independent, so the stage that existed only to move rotated K is gone. Outside the
    ; rope-store radius the old shape stays: in-place rope, then a fenced copy stage.
    (defn dth-kv-cache (ps bs geo ck cv pos)
        (if (dth-ropestore-ok? (nth geo 14) (nth geo 4) (nth geo 15))
            (do (dth-rope-store ps (nth geo 14) (nth bs 3) (nth geo 11) ck
                                (mul pos (nth geo 5)) (nth geo 3) (nth geo 4) (nth geo 15)
                                pos (nth geo 9) 0)
                (dth-copy ps (nth bs 4) cv (nth geo 5) (mul pos (nth geo 5)) 0))
            (do (dth-rope ps (nth geo 14) (nth bs 3) (nth geo 11) (nth geo 3) (nth geo 4)
                          (nth geo 15) pos (nth geo 9) 0)
                (dth-copy ps (nth bs 3) ck (nth geo 5) (mul pos (nth geo 5)) 1)
                (dth-copy ps (nth bs 4) cv (nth geo 5) (mul pos (nth geo 5)) 0))))

    ; three dispatches, two inner fences: scores must precede soft, soft must precede out. The
    ; one-thread-per-head attestant (pipe 9) stays in the unit; these are its bit-exact maps.
    (defn dth-attn (ps qh kh vh yh sh npos nq nkv hd scaleBits sstride bb)
        (do (metal_enqueue (nth ps 40)
                           (md-bind16 (list qh kh sh) (list npos nq nkv hd scaleBits sstride)
                                      256 0 0 bb)
                           (mul nq npos))
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 41)
                           (md-bind16 (list sh) (list npos nq sstride) 256 0 0 1)
                           nq)
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 42)
                           (md-bind16 (list vh sh yh) (list npos nq nkv hd sstride) 256 0 0 1)
                           (mul nq hd))))

    (defn dth-elem (ps p ah bh yh n bb)
        (metal_enqueue p (md-bind16 (list ah bh yh) (list n) 256 0 0 bb) n))

    (defn dth-copy (ps sh dh n doff bb)
        (metal_enqueue (nth ps 13) (md-bind16 (list sh dh) (list n doff) 256 0 0 bb) n))

    ; greedy selection in two stages, tie rule intact by construction (comparison and selection
    ; only — EQUALITY with the attestant): 1024 contiguous chunks, then one group folds ascending.
    (defn dth-argmax (ps bs vocabN)
        (do (metal_enqueue (nth ps 24)
                           (md-bind16 (list (nth bs 11) (nth bs 15) (nth bs 16))
                                      (list vocabN 1024) 256 0 0 1)
                           1024)
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 25)
                           (md-bind16 (list (nth bs 15) (nth bs 16) (nth bs 13) (nth bs 14))
                                      (list 1024) 1024 0 1 1)
                           1)))

    ; ================= one block =================
    ; geo: 0 dModel 1 dFF 2 nHead 3 nKV 4 headDim 5 kvd 6 maxpos 7 vocabN 8 epsBits 9 baseBits
    ;      10 scaleBits 11 ropeH 12 nLayer 13 qOut 14 ropeStyle 15 ropeDim 16 nLoop
    ; ROUND THREE'S SHAPE (2026-08-09): the wall decomposition said the small-model gap is the
    ; stage quantum times the stage count, so the block was refolded around its data
    ; dependencies with every fusion a stated map:
    ;   * the residual add rides the NEXT norm's dispatch (form_add_rmsnorm_wide_f32): each
    ;     block takes a PENDING residual handle in, adds it inside its entry norm, and returns
    ;     its ffn_down output as the next pending — two stages per block become zero.
    ;   * the three qkv biases ride their matvecs' epilogues (bflag) — one stage gone.
    ;   * rotated K stores straight into its cache row (rope_*_store), V's copy beside it in
    ;     rope-q's own stage — the copy stage gone.
    ; A llama block is now 16 dispatches in 10 fenced stages (was 19 in 14); a qwen2 block lost
    ; its bias stage too. The barrier plan still places every fence on the consumer.
    ; Returns the block's pending-residual handle.
    (defn dth-block (ps bs geo lay ck cv pos pend)
        (do
            (dth-addrms ps (nth bs 0) pend (nth lay 0) (nth bs 1) (nth geo 0) (nth geo 8) 1)
            (dth-mvbias ps (nth lay 1) (nth bs 1) (nth bs 2) (nth lay 9) 1)
            (dth-mvbias ps (nth lay 2) (nth bs 1) (nth bs 3) (nth lay 10) 0)
            (dth-mvbias ps (nth lay 3) (nth bs 1) (nth bs 4) (nth lay 11) 0)
            (dth-rope ps (nth geo 14) (nth bs 2) (nth geo 11) (nth geo 2) (nth geo 4) (nth geo 15) pos (nth geo 9) 1)
            (dth-kv-cache ps bs geo ck cv pos)
            (dth-attn ps (nth bs 2) ck cv (nth bs 5) (nth bs 12)
                      (add pos 1) (nth geo 2) (nth geo 3) (nth geo 4) (nth geo 10) (nth geo 6) 1)
            (dth-mv ps (nth lay 4) (nth bs 5) (nth bs 6) 1)
            (dth-addrms ps (nth bs 0) (nth bs 6) (nth lay 5) (nth bs 1) (nth geo 0) (nth geo 8) 1)
            (dth-mv ps (nth lay 6) (nth bs 1) (nth bs 8) 1)
            (dth-mv ps (nth lay 7) (nth bs 1) (nth bs 9) 0)
            (dth-elem ps (nth ps 10) (nth bs 8) (nth bs 9) (nth bs 10) (nth geo 1) 1)
            (dth-mv ps (nth lay 8) (nth bs 10) (nth bs 7) 1)
            (nth bs 7)))

    (defn dth-blocks (ps bs geo lays cks cvs pos l n loopoff pend)
        (if (ge l n) pend
            (dth-blocks ps bs geo lays cks cvs pos (add l 1) n loopoff
                (dth-block ps bs geo (nth lays l) (nth cks (add l loopoff))
                           (nth cvs (add l loopoff)) pos pend))))

    ; the loop passes: after every pass but the last, the pending residual folds into the FULL
    ; final norm, in place — the released nanbeige semantics (norm after each pass; the last
    ; pass's norm is the head's), the add now fused into that very dispatch. Each pass hands
    ; its successor a clean x and no pending. A one-loop file walks this once.
    (defn dth-passes (ps bs geo lays cks cvs onormTv pos lp nLoop pend)
        (if (ge lp nLoop) pend
            (do (let p2 (dth-blocks ps bs geo lays cks cvs pos 0 (nth geo 12)
                                    (mul lp (nth geo 12)) pend))
                (if (lt (add lp 1) nLoop)
                    (do (dth-addrms ps (nth bs 0) p2 onormTv (nth bs 0) (nth geo 0) (nth geo 8) 1)
                        (dth-passes ps bs geo lays cks cvs onormTv pos (add lp 1) nLoop 0))
                    (dth-passes ps bs geo lays cks cvs onormTv pos (add lp 1) nLoop p2)))))

    (defn dth-head (ps bs geo onormTv projTv pend)
        (do
            (dth-addrms ps (nth bs 0) pend onormTv (nth bs 1) (nth geo 0) (nth geo 8) 1)
            (dth-mv ps projTv (nth bs 1) (nth bs 11) 1)
            (dth-argmax ps bs (nth geo 7))
            0))

    (defn dth-u32 (s)
        (add (str_byte_at s 0)
        (add (mul (str_byte_at s 1) 256)
        (add (mul (str_byte_at s 2) 65536)
             (mul (str_byte_at s 3) 16777216)))))

    (defn dth-forward (ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv projTv id pos)
        (do
            (metal_batch_concurrent)
            (dth-dq ps embTv (nth bs 0) (mul id (nth geo 0)) (nth geo 0) 0)
            (let pend (dth-passes ps bs geo lays cks cvs onormTv pos 0 (nth geo 16) 0))
            (dth-head ps bs geo onormTv projTv pend)
            (dth-u32 (metal_buf_read (nth bs 13) 0 4))))

    (defn dth-generate (ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv projTv id pos n acc)
        (if (le n 0) acc
            (do (let nid (dth-forward ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv projTv id pos))
                (dth-generate ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv projTv
                              nid (add pos 1) (sub n 1) (append acc (list nid))))))

    (defn dth-prefill (ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv projTv ids pos)
        (if (eq (len ids) 1)
            (list (dth-forward ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv projTv (head ids) pos) pos)
            (do (dth-forward ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv projTv (head ids) pos)
                (dth-prefill ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv projTv (tail ids) (add pos 1)))))

    ; ================= the tokenizer: longest match, stated =================
    ; FORWARD byte-level map (gpt2 vocabs): a text byte to the codepoint the vocabulary spells it
    ; as, UTF-8 encoded. The inverse of l3d-uni-byte, boundary for boundary.
    (defn dtk-sub-cp (b)
        (if (le b 32) (add 256 b)
        (if (eq b 173) 323
            (add 256 (sub b 94)))))

    (defn dtk-cp-utf8 (cp)
        (if (lt cp 128) (byte_to_str cp)
            (str_concat (byte_to_str (add 192 (div cp 64)))
                        (byte_to_str (add 128 (mod cp 64))))))

    (defn dtk-gpt2-byte (b)
        (if (l3d-printable? b) (byte_to_str b) (dtk-cp-utf8 (dtk-sub-cp b))))

    (defn dtk-gpt2-walk (text i n acc)
        (if (ge i n) acc
            (dtk-gpt2-walk text (add i 1) n (str_concat acc (dtk-gpt2-byte (str_byte_at text i))))))
    (defn dtk-gpt2-map (text) (dtk-gpt2-walk text 0 (str_len text) ""))

    ; SentencePiece surface: every space becomes U+2581, and the text leads with one.
    (defn dtk-sp-walk (text i n acc)
        (if (ge i n) acc
            (dtk-sp-walk text (add i 1) n
                (str_concat acc
                    (if (eq (str_byte_at text i) 32)
                        (str_concat (byte_to_str 226) (str_concat (byte_to_str 150) (byte_to_str 129)))
                        (byte_to_str (str_byte_at text i)))))))
    (defn dtk-sp-map (text)
        (str_concat (str_concat (byte_to_str 226) (str_concat (byte_to_str 150) (byte_to_str 129)))
                    (dtk-sp-walk text 0 (str_len text) "")))

    ; does piece at cursor `at` (len L) equal text[i .. i+L)?
    (defn dtk-piece-eq (src at L text i k)
        (if (ge k L) true
            (if (eq (gmt-token-byte src at k) (str_byte_at text (add i k)))
                (dtk-piece-eq src at L text i (add k 1))
                false)))

    ; ONE vocabulary walk per text position: keep the longest piece that matches there. Ties in
    ; length keep the FIRST id — a rule, stated.
    (defn dtk-best (src at id n text i rem bestL bestId)
        (if (le n 0) (list bestId bestL)
            (do (let L (gmt-token-len src at))
                (let hit (if (gt L bestL)
                             (if (le L rem) (dtk-piece-eq src at L text i 0) false)
                             false))
                (dtk-best src (gmt-token-next src at) (add id 1) (sub n 1) text i rem
                          (if hit L bestL) (if hit id bestId)))))

    (defn dtk-ids (src vfirst vn text i n acc)
        (if (ge i n) acc
            (do (let b (dtk-best src vfirst 0 vn text i (sub n i) 0 (sub 0 1)))
                (if (lt (nth b 0) 0) acc
                    (dtk-ids src vfirst vn text (add i (nth b 1)) n (append acc (list (nth b 0))))))))

    ; text -> ids. model is the file's tokenizer.ggml.model: "gpt2" maps bytes, "llama" maps spaces.
    (defn dtk-encode (src text)
        (do (let surface (if (str_eq (gmt-str src "tokenizer.ggml.model") "llama")
                             (dtk-sp-map text)
                             (dtk-gpt2-map text)))
            (let ids (dtk-ids src (gmt-tokens-first src) (gmt-vocab-n src) surface 0
                              (str_len surface) (empty)))
            (if (eq (dth-bool src "tokenizer.ggml.add_bos_token" 1) 1)
                (append (list (gmt-u32 src "tokenizer.ggml.bos_token_id")) ids)
                ids)))

    ; ================= detokenize (SentencePiece side; gpt2 side is l3d-text) =================
    (defn dtk-sp-piece (src at L k acc)
        (if (ge k L) acc
            (do (let b (gmt-token-byte src at k))
                (if (eq b 226)
                    (if (lt (add k 2) L)
                        (if (eq (gmt-token-byte src at (add k 1)) 150)
                            (if (eq (gmt-token-byte src at (add k 2)) 129)
                                (dtk-sp-piece src at L (add k 3) (str_concat acc " "))
                                (dtk-sp-piece src at L (add k 1) (str_concat acc (byte_to_str b))))
                            (dtk-sp-piece src at L (add k 1) (str_concat acc (byte_to_str b))))
                        (dtk-sp-piece src at L (add k 1) (str_concat acc (byte_to_str b))))
                    (dtk-sp-piece src at L (add k 1) (str_concat acc (byte_to_str b)))))))

    ; one cursor walk for ALL wanted ids (ids need not be sorted; each pass scans the walk once per
    ; id — ids are few, pieces are many, so the walk is what must not repeat per id).
    (defn dtk-sp-one (src at id want)
        (if (eq id want) at
            (dtk-sp-one src (gmt-token-next src at) (add id 1) want)))

    ; SentencePiece BYTE-FALLBACK pieces spell a byte as the six characters <0xNN>. They decode to
    ; the byte, not to their spelling.
    (defn dtk-hex (c)
        (if (le c 57) (sub c 48)
            (if (le c 70) (add (sub c 65) 10) (add (sub c 97) 10))))
    (defn dtk-sp-bytepiece? (src at L)
        (if (eq L 6)
            (if (eq (gmt-token-byte src at 0) 60)
                (if (eq (gmt-token-byte src at 1) 48)
                    (if (eq (gmt-token-byte src at 2) 120)
                        (eq (gmt-token-byte src at 5) 62) false) false) false) false))
    (defn dtk-sp-render (src at L)
        (if (dtk-sp-bytepiece? src at L)
            (byte_to_str (add (mul 16 (dtk-hex (gmt-token-byte src at 3)))
                              (dtk-hex (gmt-token-byte src at 4))))
            (dtk-sp-piece src at L 0 "")))
    (defn dtk-sp-text-walk (src vfirst ids acc)
        (if (eq (len ids) 0) acc
            (do (let at (dtk-sp-one src vfirst 0 (head ids)))
                (dtk-sp-text-walk src vfirst (tail ids)
                    (str_concat acc (dtk-sp-render src at (gmt-token-len src at)))))))
    (defn dtk-sp-text (src ids) (dtk-sp-text-walk src (gmt-tokens-first src) ids ""))

    ; ================= geometry, assembled =================
    ; Everything below is READ. Returns the (geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv projTv) septet a driver
    ; needs, plus the pipes and buffers, as one list:
    ;   0 ps 1 bs 2 geo 3 lays 4 cks 5 cvs 6 embTv 7 onormTv 8 projTv 9 arch 10 src
    (defn dth-open (path maxpos ropeStyleOverride)
        (do
            (let src (dth-src path))
            (let arch (gmt-str src "general.architecture"))
            (let tab (dth-table src))
            (let base (egg-data-base src (dth-alignment)))
            (let nLayer (gmt-u32 src (dth-key arch "block_count")))
            (let dModel (gmt-u32 src (dth-key arch "embedding_length")))
            (let dFF (gmt-u32 src (dth-key arch "feed_forward_length")))
            (let nHead (gmt-u32 src (dth-key arch "attention.head_count")))
            (let nKV (gmt-u32 src (dth-key arch "attention.head_count_kv")))
            (let headDim (dth-u32-or src (dth-key arch "attention.key_length") (div dModel nHead)))
            (let ropeDim (dth-u32-or src (dth-key arch "rope.dimension_count") headDim))
            (let nLoop (dth-u32-or src (dth-key arch "num_loops") 1))
            (let ropeBase (gmt-f32 src (dth-key arch "rope.freq_base")))
            (let rmsEps (gmt-f32 src (dth-key arch "attention.layer_norm_rms_epsilon")))
            (let kvd (mul nKV headDim))
            (let qOut (mul nHead headDim))
            ; qwen2's rope is half-split; llama-arch files were permuted for adjacent pairs at
            ; conversion. -1 asks the arch; 0/1 force a style so a band can PROBE an undeclared file.
            (let style (if (ge ropeStyleOverride 0) ropeStyleOverride
                           (if (str_eq arch "qwen2") 1 0)))
            (let projTv0 (dth-out-tv tab base path))
            (let vocabN (dth-tv-r projTv0))
            (let ps (dth-pipes (dth-msl)))
            (let bs (dth-bufs dModel dFF qOut kvd vocabN nHead maxpos))
            (let lays (dth-layers tab base path 0 nLayer (empty)))
            (let cks (dth-cache (mul nLayer nLoop) kvd maxpos (empty)))
            (let cvs (dth-cache (mul nLayer nLoop) kvd maxpos (empty)))
            (let embTv (dth-tv tab base path "token_embd.weight"))
            (let onormTv (dth-tv tab base path "output_norm.weight"))
            (let ropeH (dth-rope-freqs tab base path (div headDim 2)))
            (let geo (list dModel dFF nHead nKV headDim kvd maxpos vocabN
                           (md-f32-bits rmsEps) (md-f32-bits ropeBase)
                           (md-f32-bits (div 1.0 (math_sqrt (add headDim 0.0))))
                           ropeH nLayer qOut style ropeDim nLoop))
            (list ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv projTv0 arch src)))

    ; ================= the phi2 shape: parallel residual, LayerNorm, fused qkv =================
    ; One norm per block feeds BOTH arms, and the residual adds both:
    ;   x = x + attn_out(attn(rope(split(qkv(ln(x)))))) + ffn_down(gelu(ffn_up(ln(x))))
    ; The rope is half-split over the first rope.dimension_count dims (32 of 64), the norm is
    ; MEAN-CENTERED with gain and bias, the activation is GELU, and every projection carries a
    ; bias. eps is <arch>.attention.layer_norm_epsilon — the LN key, not the RMS key.

    (defn dth-f32-or (src key dflt)
        (do (let v (gmt-f32 src key))
            (if (eq v (gmt-absent)) dflt v)))

    ; ten entries per layer: norm w/b, qkv w/b, attn_output w/b, ffn_up w/b, ffn_down w/b
    (defn dth-p2-layer (tab base path l)
        (list (dth-tv tab base path (dth-blk l "attn_norm.weight"))
              (dth-tv tab base path (dth-blk l "attn_norm.bias"))
              (dth-tv tab base path (dth-blk l "attn_qkv.weight"))
              (dth-tv tab base path (dth-blk l "attn_qkv.bias"))
              (dth-tv tab base path (dth-blk l "attn_output.weight"))
              (dth-tv tab base path (dth-blk l "attn_output.bias"))
              (dth-tv tab base path (dth-blk l "ffn_up.weight"))
              (dth-tv tab base path (dth-blk l "ffn_up.bias"))
              (dth-tv tab base path (dth-blk l "ffn_down.weight"))
              (dth-tv tab base path (dth-blk l "ffn_down.bias"))))

    (defn dth-p2-layers (tab base path l n acc)
        (if (ge l n) acc
            (dth-p2-layers tab base path (add l 1) n (append acc (list (dth-p2-layer tab base path l))))))

    ; bufs: 0 X 1 Xb 2 QKV 3 Q 4 Ks 5 Vs 6 Attn 7 Proj 8 Ffn 9 Up 10 Act 11 Logits 12 Scratch
    ;       13 OutI 14 OutV
    (defn dth-p2-bufs (dModel dFF vocabN nHead maxpos kvd)
        (list (metal_buf_alloc (mul dModel 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul dModel 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul dModel 3) 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul dModel 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul kvd 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul kvd 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul dModel 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul dModel 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul dModel 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul dFF 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul dFF 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul vocabN 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul (mul 2 nHead) maxpos) 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc 16)
              (metal_buf_alloc 16)
              (metal_buf_alloc 4096)
              (metal_buf_alloc 4096)))

    ; the parallel residual's two adds ride the next LayerNorm's dispatch (pipe 47) the same
    ; way the dense path's single add rides pipe 46: x = (x + attn) + ffn in the attestant's
    ; own association, then form_layernorm_wide_f32's body unchanged. aflag=0 (the first
    ; block — x is the embedding) binds bs7/bs8 unread and IS the wide LayerNorm.
    (defn dth-p2-addln (ps xh h1 h2 gtv btv yh n epsBits aflag bb)
        (metal_enqueue (nth ps 47)
                       (md-bind16 (list xh h1 h2 (dth-tv-h gtv) (dth-tv-h btv) yh)
                                  (list n epsBits aflag) 256 0 1 bb) 1))
    (defn dth-p2-slice (ps sh dh n soff bb)
        (metal_enqueue (nth ps 22) (md-bind16 (list sh dh) (list n soff) 256 0 0 bb) n))
    (defn dth-p2-gelu (ps xh yh n bb)
        (metal_enqueue (nth ps 21) (md-bind16 (list xh yh) (list n) 256 0 0 bb) n))

    ; geo as dth-open lays it; style is 1 (half-split) by the arch's own build, rd = 32 of hd 64
    ; — INSIDE the unrotated-tail radius, so the in-place rope + copy stay dispatched here.
    ; Round three's fusions applied: both residual adds ride the next LayerNorm (aflag), every
    ; bias rides its matvec's epilogue. A phi2 block is 14 dispatches in 10 fenced stages
    ; (was 21 in 16). aflag is the pending mark: 0 only for the first block.
    (defn dth-p2-block (ps bs geo lay ck cv pos aflag)
        (do
            (dth-p2-addln ps (nth bs 0) (nth bs 7) (nth bs 8) (nth lay 0) (nth lay 1)
                          (nth bs 1) (nth geo 0) (nth geo 8) aflag 1)
            (dth-mvbias ps (nth lay 2) (nth bs 1) (nth bs 2) (nth lay 3) 1)
            (dth-p2-slice ps (nth bs 2) (nth bs 3) (nth geo 0) 0 1)
            (dth-p2-slice ps (nth bs 2) (nth bs 4) (nth geo 5) (nth geo 0) 0)
            (dth-p2-slice ps (nth bs 2) (nth bs 5) (nth geo 5) (mul (nth geo 0) 2) 0)
            (dth-rope ps 1 (nth bs 3) (nth geo 11) (nth geo 2) (nth geo 4) (nth geo 15) pos (nth geo 9) 1)
            (dth-rope ps 1 (nth bs 4) (nth geo 11) (nth geo 3) (nth geo 4) (nth geo 15) pos (nth geo 9) 0)
            (dth-copy ps (nth bs 4) ck (nth geo 5) (mul pos (nth geo 5)) 1)
            (dth-copy ps (nth bs 5) cv (nth geo 5) (mul pos (nth geo 5)) 0)
            (dth-attn ps (nth bs 3) ck cv (nth bs 6) (nth bs 12)
                      (add pos 1) (nth geo 2) (nth geo 3) (nth geo 4) (nth geo 10) (nth geo 6) 1)
            (dth-mvbias ps (nth lay 4) (nth bs 6) (nth bs 7) (nth lay 5) 1)
            (dth-mvbias ps (nth lay 6) (nth bs 1) (nth bs 9) (nth lay 7) 0)
            (dth-p2-gelu ps (nth bs 9) (nth bs 10) (nth geo 1) 1)
            (dth-mvbias ps (nth lay 8) (nth bs 10) (nth bs 8) (nth lay 9) 1)
            1))

    (defn dth-p2-blocks (ps bs geo lays cks cvs pos l n aflag)
        (if (ge l n) aflag
            (do (dth-p2-block ps bs geo (nth lays l) (nth cks l) (nth cvs l) pos aflag)
                (dth-p2-blocks ps bs geo lays cks cvs pos (add l 1) n 1))))

    (defn dth-p2-head (ps bs geo onormTv onormB projTv projB aflag)
        (do
            (dth-p2-addln ps (nth bs 0) (nth bs 7) (nth bs 8) onormTv onormB
                          (nth bs 1) (nth geo 0) (nth geo 8) aflag 1)
            (dth-mvbias ps projTv (nth bs 1) (nth bs 11) projB 1)
            (dth-argmax ps bs (nth geo 7))
            0))

    (defn dth-p2-forward (ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv onormB projTv projB id pos)
        (do
            (metal_batch_concurrent)
            (dth-dq ps embTv (nth bs 0) (mul id (nth geo 0)) (nth geo 0) 0)
            (let af (dth-p2-blocks ps bs geo lays cks cvs pos 0 (nth geo 12) 0))
            (dth-p2-head ps bs geo onormTv onormB projTv projB af)
            (dth-u32 (metal_buf_read (nth bs 13) 0 4))))

    (defn dth-p2-generate (ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv onormB projTv projB id pos n acc)
        (if (le n 0) acc
            (do (let nid (dth-p2-forward ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv onormB projTv projB id pos))
                (dth-p2-generate ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv onormB projTv projB
                                 nid (add pos 1) (sub n 1) (append acc (list nid))))))

    (defn dth-p2-prefill (ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv onormB projTv projB ids pos)
        (if (eq (len ids) 1)
            (list (dth-p2-forward ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv onormB projTv projB (head ids) pos) pos)
            (do (dth-p2-forward ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv onormB projTv projB (head ids) pos)
                (dth-p2-prefill ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv onormB projTv projB (tail ids) (add pos 1)))))

    ; open for the phi2 shape:
    ;   0 ps 1 bs 2 geo 3 lays 4 cks 5 cvs 6 embTv 7 onormTv 8 onormB 9 projTv 10 projB 11 arch 12 src
    (defn dth-p2-open (path maxpos)
        (do
            (let src (dth-src path))
            (let arch (gmt-str src "general.architecture"))
            (let tab (dth-table src))
            (let base (egg-data-base src (dth-alignment)))
            (let nLayer (gmt-u32 src (dth-key arch "block_count")))
            (let dModel (gmt-u32 src (dth-key arch "embedding_length")))
            (let dFF (gmt-u32 src (dth-key arch "feed_forward_length")))
            (let nHead (gmt-u32 src (dth-key arch "attention.head_count")))
            (let nKV (gmt-u32 src (dth-key arch "attention.head_count_kv")))
            (let headDim (div dModel nHead))
            (let ropeDim (dth-u32-or src (dth-key arch "rope.dimension_count") headDim))
            (let ropeBase (dth-f32-or src (dth-key arch "rope.freq_base") 10000.0))
            (let lnEps (gmt-f32 src (dth-key arch "attention.layer_norm_epsilon")))
            (let kvd (mul nKV headDim))
            (let projTv0 (dth-out-tv tab base path))
            (let vocabN (dth-tv-r projTv0))
            (let ps (dth-pipes (dth-msl)))
            (let bs (dth-p2-bufs dModel dFF vocabN nHead maxpos kvd))
            (let lays (dth-p2-layers tab base path 0 nLayer (empty)))
            (let cks (dth-cache nLayer kvd maxpos (empty)))
            (let cvs (dth-cache nLayer kvd maxpos (empty)))
            (let embTv (dth-tv tab base path "token_embd.weight"))
            (let onormTv (dth-tv tab base path "output_norm.weight"))
            (let onormB (dth-tv tab base path "output_norm.bias"))
            (let projB (dth-tv tab base path "output.bias"))
            (let ropeH (dth-rope-freqs tab base path (div headDim 2)))
            (let geo (list dModel dFF nHead nKV headDim kvd maxpos vocabN
                           (md-f32-bits lnEps) (md-f32-bits ropeBase)
                           (md-f32-bits (div 1.0 (math_sqrt (add headDim 0.0))))
                           ropeH nLayer (mul nHead headDim) 1 ropeDim 1))
            (list ps bs geo lays cks cvs embTv onormTv onormB projTv0 projB arch src)))
    0)
